# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000700> (p-value)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000700> "A hypothesis testing measure that represents the probability of obtaining a result at least as far from the value actually obtained as the value expected, assuming the null hypothesis is true."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000700> "Within the frequentist framework, a p-value is typically a p-value for two-sided test and the criterion for rejecting the null hypothesis is typically expressed as a p-value that is less than an alpha setting divided by 2. In some cases, the p-value is a p-value for one-sided test, and the criterion for rejecting the null hypothesis is typically expressed as a p-value that is less than an alpha setting. A p-value is preferably coded more precisely as a p-value for two-sided test or a p-value for one-sided test rather than using the code for p-value without specification. The code for p-value (without specification) may be used in contexts where the p-value reported is ambiguous.

Within the Bayesian framework, use the posterior predictive p-value."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000700> "P value"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000700> "P-value"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000700> "PValue"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000700> "p value"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000700> "SEVCO group"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000700> "p-value"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000700> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000071>)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000700> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000057>))
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000700> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000312> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000673>))

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000713> (type I error)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000713> "the event of incorrectly rejecting the null hypothesis"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000713> "Incorrectly rejecting the null hypothesis' means rejecting the null hypothesis when it is actually true. In statistical hypothesis testing, the event of incorrectly rejecting the null hypothesis is usually not directly verifiable because it is not generally observable whether the null hypothesis is actually true.
The probability of a type I error is designated as alpha.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000713> "Brian S. Alper, Harold Lehmann, Kenneth Wilkins, Joanne Dehnbostel, Muhammad Afzal")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000117> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000713> "Philippe Rocca-Serra")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000713> "false positive error")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000713> "type 1 error")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000713> "type I error"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000713> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000242>)

